{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773074942,"nonce":"JLOtZtTRLSC3fHgPP3vKPRiSiKg=","title":"Training panel: trajectory viewer component not connected to live snapshots","message":"The worker emits real `training_trajectory` SSE events with actual arm effector positions every `snapshot_interval` batches. `useTraining` captures these into `trainingStore.latestTrajectory`. But no UI component reads from `latestTrajectory` — the data pipeline is complete end-to-end but the viewer is unimplemented.\n\n## What is needed\n\nA 2D trajectory viewer embedded in (or near) the TrainingPanel that:\n- Reads `latestTrajectory` from `trainingStore`\n- Renders the effector path as a 2D line (x/y in metres, workspace roughly 0–0.5 m)\n- Shows the target as a dot\n- Updates live as new snapshots arrive during training\n\n## Data shape (from trainingStore)\n```ts\nlatestTrajectory: {\n  batch: number;\n  effector: [number, number][];  // [[x,y], ...] length N_STEPS\n  target: [number, number];\n  t: number[];\n}\n```\n\n## Notes\n- Effector coords are in metres (workspace ~0–0.5 m square)\n- N_STEPS = cfg.n_reach_steps (default 80), CONTROL_DT = 0.01 s → 0.8 s episodes\n- Worker falls back to synthetic trajectory if eval rollout fails (non-fatal)\n- SVG is simplest renderer; no 3D needed for 2D reaching task","files":null}]}